{"name":"Austere","hex":"#726848","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"austere","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Grim or severe in manner or appearance.","Lacking decoration; trivial; not extravagant or gaudy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/austere"}],"entries":[{"title":"Austere (EDM group)","blocks":[{"text":"Austere is an anonymous electronic music group known for producing work in a range of styles including classical minimalism, psybient, ambient, dark ambient, drone, glitch-ambient, and downtempo drum and bass. The group began collaborating in 1997, with their first release issued on January 1, 1998. Although they maintain anonymity, they are loosely based in Portland, Oregon, through an affiliation with Sound-O-Mat Recordings."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austere_(EDM_group)"},{"title":"Austere (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Austere is an EP by Sparta, released in 2002 on DreamWorks Records. Their first record, it was released one year after the break-up of At the Drive-In."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/35/Austere_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austere_(EP)"},{"title":"Austere (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Austere\" is the debut single by Welsh alternative rock band The Joy Formidable. It was originally released in August 2008 on 7\" vinyl on the Another Music=Another Kitchen label. The song and band gained much exposure when YouTube removed a fan-made music video. An official video was put together featuring the band playing pass the parcel. The single was re-released for their debut album The Big Roar and a new video was made, featuring the band performing the song."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ac/Austerejoyformidable.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austere_(song)"}]